<title>SRI LANKA: S.LANKA EXPECTS $43 MLN MALAYSIA INVESTMENT.</title>
<headline>S.LANKA EXPECTS $43 MLN MALAYSIA INVESTMENT.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-08-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka expects to receive nearly $43 million Malaysian investment in various property development and infrastructure projects, including a new highway, the independent Island newspaper said on Sunday.</p>
<p>It said construction group Renong Bhd and Berjaya Land were among the Malaysian companies planning to invest in Sri Lanka.</p>
<p>The newspaper said a cement plant was also expected to be built in the Indian Ocean island using Malaysian money.</p>
<p>Sri Lankan President Chandrika Kumaratunga Bandaranaike is expected to make an official visit to Malaysia shortly, and the newpspaper said the projects were likely to be finalised before she left for Kuala Lumpur.</p>
</text>
